      "content": "Example: if Statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Let's take a look at an example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "content": "1# Check eligibility for discount.\n2\n3total = float(input(\"Enter the total amount: \"))\n4\n5# Check if total is greater than 100\n6if total > 100:\n7    print(\"Congratulations!\")\n8    print(\"You are eligible for a discount\")"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "This program behaves differently depending on the input."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Sample Output 1"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "content": "Enter the total amount: 120\nCongratulations!\nYou are eligible for a discount."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "If the user enters 120, total > 100 evaluates to True. In this case, the statements inside the if block are executed."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Sample Output 2"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "content": "Enter the total amount: 35"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "If the user enters 35, total > 100 evaluates to False. In this case, the statements inside the if block are skipped and not executed."
    },
